  "body_html": "<h1>Target Lattice Block Splitting</h1>\n<p>Let \\(L'\\) be the lattice function attached to the target point \\(x''\\), and set\n\\[\n{}^iL'_t=L'_t\\cap{}^iV'\\qquad i=b,a.\n\\]\nThen\n\\[\n{}^bL'_t={}^bw({}^bL_{t+s}),\n\\qquad\nL'={}^bL'\\oplus{}^aL',\n\\]\nand \\({}^aL'\\) is self-dual.</p>",
  "proof_html": "<p>The first identity follows from the one-block lattice transfer lemma applied to the top block, together with the inclusion \\(w\\in B_{x,x'',s}\\) and duality in \\({}^bV'\\). For the direct-sum statement, decompose \\(v\\in L'_t\\) into its \\({}^bV'\\)- and \\({}^aV'\\)-components and use the dual lattice inequalities to place each component in the corresponding block lattice. Self-duality of \\(L'\\) and of \\({}^bL'\\) then forces self-duality of \\({}^aL'\\).</p>",
